title The seventeenth rung stays home, and a lantern that fired three times becomes a check
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first under Standfast, deep-read one council-rota row, refresh the live card, and send.
think Standfast opened the lap. tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish sang GREEN at 108 and tools/glow_tend_era_suite.rish ran GREEN at ten rungs at HEAD before a line moved, both run rather than trusted. crux/REDS.md read closed through %131 with no agent-closable red standing.
think The running thread came off the top rows of session-logs/README.md. The newest recommend named redress_the_meeting at sixteen identical bodies over seventeen declarations -- 645 by realized fall, zero widening -- and asked the lap to open by reading which rung differs and why.
think Ran tools/fixtures/ladder_reach_visibility_scan.sh redress_the_meeting first. REACH_OK named folding=16 widens=0 stub=3 fall=645, and hashing the seventeen bodies with sha256sum gave two digests: sixteen at one, caravan/redress.rye alone at another.
think Diffed the odd rung against the cohort. Seven lines differ and nothing else does -- redress.rye writes report_out.redressed where the sixteen write redress_of(report_out).redressed, because in that rung the redress report IS the report and no accessor stands between them. That is meaning rather than accident, so the rung keeps its own body.
think The harness gained pub fn redress_the_meeting(comptime rung: type, io: std.Io, redress: rung.Redress, upshot: rung.Upshot, report_out: *rung.Report) (rung.RunError || rung.NoteError)!void, reaching thirteen helpers -- meeting_written, redress_of, hollow_meetings, redressed_in, closed_bare_in, upshot_earned, settlement_published, redress_bytes, redress_answers, redress_refusal, redress_note, redress_written, redress_holds -- through the type handed in.
think The stub loop globbed caravan/*.rye and filtered only caravan/redress.rye, so it swept caravan/ladder_checks.rye in with the rungs and replaced the body it had just received with a stub calling itself. The loop printed seventeen where REACH_OK had named sixteen, which is what caught it, and the harness was restored before any build.
think That is the third firing of one lantern in this arc. The say_the_word lap recorded a glob overwriting the harness with its own stub; the meet_the_debt lap wrote that its stub loop excluded the harness by name this time rather than by luck. Both repaired by hand, both written into a log, neither into a tool. Booked as REDS %132 and closed with a guard rather than a fourth careful hand.
think The guard reads caravan/ladder_checks.rye for a line whose body is return ladder_checks. and refuses verdict=harness_delegates_to_itself, placed ahead of the measurement because a clobbered harness leaves every rung's stub intact and would otherwise answer verdict=ok about a tree that no longer compiles. The control is a throwaway ladder holding one self-delegating function, so the living harness is never touched to prove the refusal.
think Three living claims moved with the code. The carry scan's ceiling came down 73,167 to 72,522, the carry witness's two pinned lines moved to the measured carry and body counts, and the reach-visibility witness advanced one lap -- folded slot redress_the_meeting, head slot weigh_the_answer, sibling slot confirm_pruned.
think Two stale prose claims were found beside them and repaired to read rather than recite. The carry witness's fold-queue paragraph still narrated the ask_path lap two folds back, and era rung ten recited 2,141 pure delegating stubs where the scan reads 2,315 -- a drift of exactly 174, the six folds landed since that sentence was typed. Both now name the scan's own output rather than a number a hand carried.
obs Prediction met measurement to the digit for the fourth lap running under the meter. Carry 73,161 -> 72,516, a fall of exactly 645; delegates 2,999 -> 3,015, exactly the sixteen stubs; bodies 18,167 -> 18,168; distinct 7,964 -> 7,965; ceiling down to 72,522.
obs The derivation is fifteen bodies times forty-three lines. One body survives in the harness and each stub costs three, so a family folding n at k lines returns (n-1)(k-3).
obs Run against the folded family afterward the same scan reads widens=16 fall=0 -- a stub reaches ladder_checks, private in each rung -- so the queue reports a door already through rather than offering it twice.
obs The split-on-one-qualifier shape has now appeared three laps running, and six times across the arc: deem, owe, avow, meet, apprise, and now redress. Every one turned out to be meaning. A cohort is read at the head of the lap and its outliers are read for what they say.
obs The 2,141 recital is the same fault as REDS %130 in a quieter place. A number a meter prints survives a wrong sentence; a number a hand describes drifts silently for six laps. The repair is the same one both times: the sentence names the measurement rather than repeating it.
obs Council rota, row two -- Fire and Mars, cut and stop. The row priced this lap exactly. Standfast named the shape of the harness catch: the loop reported seventeen where the meter had named sixteen, and the honest move was to stop and read rather than build over a count that disagreed. Reds-first named the repair: a lantern that fires twice becomes a loom, and this one had fired three times while two logs recorded it and no tool learned it. And the three depths of removal placed the fold itself -- a lift is gentler than the gentlest depth named there, since a body moving into one home removes nothing and every rung keeps its own name at the door.
